## What a real nougat.mmd would contain (if paper.pdf were available)

If the BBRC 2024 PDF were on disk, this file would be the output of

```
nougat paper.pdf -o extraction/ -m 0.1.0-base --recompute
```

producing a Markdown-with-math extraction of the full paper: title, authors, abstract, all
section text (Intro / Methods / Results / Discussion / Conclusion), all figure captions, all
tables, and all equations in LaTeX form. That extraction is a hard prerequisite for
claim-level verification against the smoke model.

Because the paper is not on disk, downstream claim-extraction (`notes/claims.md`) was
performed against the PubMed abstract + MeSH headings + author keywords only, and is
explicitly noted as inference-from-abstract throughout REPORT.md and REPORT.tex.

